  "names": {
    "order": "given family",
    "conventions": "Saudis carry their own name, bin (son of) or bint (daughter of) their father's name, the grandfather's name, then the family or tribal name, usually with Al, as in Abdullah bin Saad Al Qahtani or Sara bint Fahad Al Otaibi. On a badge or in a meeting it is the first name and family name, and women keep their own family name after marriage. Older men are often called by kunya, Abu plus the eldest son's name (Abu Fahad), and women Umm plus the son's name. Egyptians, Yemenis and Levantines use Arabic names with a father's or family name; South Asians and Filipinos keep their home conventions.",
